   "line": 3,
   "text": "The sound going into the phone is the true tone, a smooth wobble. But a phone only works with numbers. Eight thousand times a second, it takes one sample. That's the sampling rate. In between, it looks away. The list of samples is what the phone stores, and nothing else survives.",
