  {
   "line": 7,
   "text": "Sweep the true tone up. The stored tone climbs with it to four thousand hertz, then turns round. That's the limit, half the sampling rate. Above it, the phone stores a lower, false tone with the same samples, an alias. Fold the strip at the limit. Five thousand sits one thousand above. [surprise-oh] So it lands one thousand below, on three thousand.",
